			<div class="content" id="post-content-403147">
									

<p>The way I understand it, Euclid stuff is weird, freaky stuff that has a not-insignificant chance of doing bad things to you if handled without proper safety measures, but probably won't kill you if you're smart about how you interact with it. Keter stuff is stuff that kills and maims pretty much by default, often intentionally (or that, like you said, threatens the world). The wolves in your example, assuming they possessed some abnormal trait that separated them from normal wolves, could very well be classed as Keter if they went around depopulating villages.</p>

